WEBVTT

00:00.180 --> 00:01.170
Instructor: All right, so hopefully,

00:01.170 --> 00:02.580
you now have Git installed.

00:02.580 --> 00:04.410
We're now moving on to what is probably

00:04.410 --> 00:07.740
the most essential section in this course.

00:07.740 --> 00:10.380
We're talking about some of the core Git commands

00:10.380 --> 00:13.350
so there's going to be a lot in the Critical column here.

00:13.350 --> 00:15.540
First, we're gonna talk about this concept

00:15.540 --> 00:19.110
of GI Repositories, Repos for short, what are they?

00:19.110 --> 00:21.930
And then we'll learn a bunch of commands, GI Init,

00:21.930 --> 00:24.240
that's going to be critical, and Git Status.

00:24.240 --> 00:27.813
These are things you'll use nonstop if you use Git.

00:29.001 --> 00:31.860
Understanding the .git folder I'll say is important,

00:31.860 --> 00:33.180
but not a critical thing.

00:33.180 --> 00:35.040
You could go your whole life as a GI user

00:35.040 --> 00:38.370
without really understanding it and what's inside of it.

00:38.370 --> 00:41.730
The Committing Workflow, a very important concept,

00:41.730 --> 00:43.770
sort of an overview that we'll do.

00:43.770 --> 00:46.110
And then we'll dive into three more commands,

00:46.110 --> 00:48.235
Git Add, Git Commit, and Git Log.

00:48.235 --> 00:52.020
None of them are terribly difficult or anything like that,

00:52.020 --> 00:54.660
but they are very, very important,

00:54.660 --> 00:56.460
essential to working with Git

00:56.460 --> 00:58.680
and they'll come up throughout the rest of the course.

00:58.680 --> 01:00.450
So take your time with this section.

01:00.450 --> 01:01.680
Don't speed through it.

01:01.680 --> 01:04.590
Remember how much is in the Critical column.

01:04.590 --> 01:07.740
Because for future sections, that really won't be the case.

01:07.740 --> 01:09.540
So let's go ahead and get started.

01:09.540 --> 01:11.220
What really matters? Pretty much everything.

01:11.220 --> 01:12.273
Okay, here we go.
